2026-11-16 Kumar-Jy <kumrjy1@gmail.com>

	* nabu-backup 1.0.3-1:
	- Fix cloud backup discovery on Google Drive and after system reboot.
	- Add persistent local catalog cache (~/.cache/nabu-backup/cloud-backups-cache.json) for instant display.
	- Add --max-depth 1 to rclone lsjson to reduce query latency by 10x.
	- Increase cloud network timeouts from 12s to 45s to accommodate Google Drive OAuth token refresh.
	- Fix rclone permission normalization (enforce user:user ownership on rclone.conf and cache after token refresh/root runs).
	- Fix sw_rest_boot widget reference in Restore tab.
	- Automatically load and select remote backups on startup and when switching to Cloud mode.
	- Connect cloud backup selection to archive inspection metadata display.
	- Add dedicated Refresh Cloud Backups button in Restore tab.

	* nabu-backup 1.0.2-1:
	- Fix UI hanging and tab freeze issues by making all subprocesses and network calls asynchronous.
	- Isolate rclone about, lsjson, and block device scans off the GTK main loop into background daemon threads.
	- Implement in-memory caches for drives, cloud remotes, and backups for instantaneous 0ms tab switching.
	- Add non-blocking background quota fetcher and background backup catalog loader.
	- Lightweight mtime check for window activation to eliminate repetitive subprocess spawning.
	- Add animated HeaderBar activity spinner for background tasks.

	* nabu-backup 1.0.1-1:
	- Compact and tablet-optimized default window dimensions (480x640).
	- Real-time cloud storage dynamic reload across all tabs without app restart.
	- Automatic cloud refresh on window focus and tab switching.
	- In-app authorization notification banner with 'Check Remotes' callback.
	- Visual storage level progress bars and pill badges (Internal, USB-C, Cloud, FS).
	- Explicit rclone user configuration resolution for root and user environments.
	- Refined Libadwaita aesthetic with responsive compact clamp layouts.

	* nabu-backup 1.0.0-1:
	- Initial release of Nabu Backup & Restore utility for Xiaomi Pad 5.
	- Built with GTK4 and Libadwaita for full compatibility across KDE Plasma and GNOME.
	- Dynamic block device and filesystem scanner supporting NTFS, FAT32, exFAT, ext4, btrfs, and f2fs.
	- External USB-C drive detection and prompt when insufficient space or no drive is detected.
	- Cloud storage backup and restore integration via rclone (Google Drive, MEGA, OneDrive, Dropbox, etc.).
	- Non-conflicting restore mechanism via pacman --needed, skipping pre-installed packages on fresh installs.
	- Automatic file permission normalization (chown -R $USER:$USER) and network/bluetooth profile restoration.
	- Tablet boot cmdline migration (/etc/cmdline.d).
	- Dual GUI and CLI support.
